+   pauses down to 0.1 s, 0.06 s of air before a line, 0.12 s after — **but never a shot under 0.8 s inside one take**
+   (Eyad, 1 Oct: a 0.44 s shot left by cutting a tiny pause "looks like a weird visual stutter"; the pause stays
+   instead, and check.py fails it) — `pauses.py` (new jobs) or `pauses.py --edit` (re-tighten a job;
    also moves the first cut past the director and remaps card times). The end CTA stays on screen ≥ 1.8 s: keep the
    silent hold after "below"; if something off his mic is in it, `"mute_after"` silences his mic there instead.
 5. **Frame 1 carries the title and the logo.**
