 | Element | Now |
 |---|---|
 | Captions | **Last line on baseline 1450, extra lines stack upward** — under his beard, just above the logo (Sofian, 30 Sep). Inter Tight 700, 72 px, white, strong 3-pass drop shadow. ALL-CAPS and numbers → Playfair 800 white with a red underline that draws in (honorifics SWT/SAW/PBUH stay plain). **Never the Pinyon script.** 1–3 words per chunk, broken on phrases; each word appears as he says it; the chunk is laid out once so nothing shifts |
-| Title (hook) | Top of frame over a soft black scrim: **every line the same Inter Tight 700 at 64 px, the question line included** (Sofian, 30 Sep: "the question and the text are different sizes"); `*marked*` words look like the rest, `_MARKED_` keeps a red underline. ≤ 22 characters a line. Fades at `hook_until` (end of the first sentence, before the first card at 25 s) |
+| Title (hook) | Top of frame over a soft black scrim: **every line the same face and size** (Sofian, 30 Sep). **No question marks** (Eyad, 1 Oct; check.py fails them). Face per video, switched up across the account: `"hook_font": "sans"` (Inter Tight 700, 64 px) or `"serif"` (the end CTA's Playfair 800, 66 px, lining figures) — the serif is for titles only, never captions (Eyad, 1 Oct). `*marked*` words look like the rest, `_MARKED_` keeps a red underline. ≤ 22 characters a line. Fades at `hook_until` (end of the first sentence, before the first card at 25 s) |
 | Logo | Red `CEOwills` (Arimo 700, `#EB1519`, 392 px wide, baseline 1600), centred on its ink, every frame, over a black bottom gradient **from y 1300 down** (the layer doubled) — behind the captions and logo only, like ExamQA (Sofian, 30 Sep: "the gradient is so high"; it used to start at 1000, across his chest) |
 | Frame | **Zoomed 1.08× and moved down up to 190 px** (Sofian, 30 Sep) so there's room above his head. Per cut, render.py tracks his head and fills the space with **only the wall above his hair**, stretched (no blurred copy of the frame — that put a ghost head above him and blurred his hair). A cut where he leans to the top of the shot gets less shift, or none; a cut where he leans in gets less so his beard stays above the captions (`frame` in layout.json, `shifts` in boxes.json) |
 | iMessage cards | **Real-size iPhone banners** (Sofian/Eyad, 30 Sep: "so small it looks unrealistic"): 1000 px wide at y 100, Adnan's contact photo (his face from the video) with the Messages badge, "Adnan · now", frosted glass, ceowills.com in red, drawn by render.py (`notify.style: ios`). Slide down, 6 s each, first at 25 s then every 30 s, never over the end CTA, none in reels under 30 s, notification sound on each. **Text written for what he's saying at that moment, different in every video** — see below |
diff --git a/tools/ceowills/check.py b/tools/ceowills/check.py
index e4d5623..1487f21 100644
--- a/tools/ceowills/check.py
+++ b/tools/ceowills/check.py
@@ -45,7 +45,11 @@ def main():
         except Exception: fail(f"raw video won't open (incomplete download?): {E['video']}")
     for i, c in enumerate(E.get("cuts", [])):
         if c["out"] <= c["in"]: fail(f"cut {i}: out {c['out']} ≤ in {c['in']}")
-        elif c["out"] - c["in"] < L["cuts"]["min_clip_s"]: warn(f"cut {i} is only {c['out'] - c['in']:.2f} s — a flash cut?")
+        elif c["out"] - c["in"] < L["cuts"]["min_clip_s"]:
+            # a short shot that only removed a small pause inside one take reads as a stutter (#2 v7 at 1:25, 1 Oct)
+            near = ([c["in"] - E["cuts"][i - 1]["out"]] if i else []) + ([E["cuts"][i + 1]["in"] - c["out"]] if i + 1 < len(E["cuts"]) else [])
+            gap = min([g for g in near if g >= 0], default=9)   # a negative gap = re-ordered words, on purpose
+            (fail if 0 <= gap <= 0.35 else warn)(f"cut {i} is only {c['out'] - c['in']:.2f} s" + (f" and {gap:.2f} s from its neighbour — merge it (a jump cut for a tiny pause looks like a stutter)" if 0 <= gap <= 0.35 else " — a flash cut? fine only if it's a whole word or line on purpose"))
     segs, dur, to_out = render.timeline(E.get("cuts", []), fps)
     if not segs: fail("no cuts")
     lo, hi = L["length"]["target_s"]
@@ -84,6 +88,8 @@ def main():
         for line in hook:
             plain = re.sub(r"[*_]", "", line)
             if len(plain) > 22: warn(f"title line '{plain}' is {len(plain)} characters (≤ 22 keeps it big)")
+            if "?" in plain: fail(f"title line '{plain}' has a question mark — titles have none (Eyad, 1 Oct)")
+        if E.get("hook_font", "sans") not in ("sans", "serif"): fail(f"hook_font '{E['hook_font']}' — use sans or serif")
         hu = E.get("hook_until")
         hu_out = to_out(hu) if hu is not None else dur
         if hu is not None and hu_out is None: fail(f"hook_until {hu} is not inside a kept cut")
